# Environment variables — copy this file to .env
#
# The OpenAI API key is NO LONGER stored in the app. AI requests are routed to a
# backend proxy that holds the key server-side. Configure the proxy at build
# time with a Dart define (not via .env):
#
#   flutter run --dart-define=API_BASE_URL=https://your-backend.example.com
#
# See lib/core/network/ai_gateway.dart. An app attestation token header is sent
# with every AI call (wired to Firebase App Check in a later task).
#
# The .env file is still loaded for other runtime config (e.g. Google sign-in
# client id), so keep it in place.
